div.p:
“But while the fore legs advance the body by drawing the free lever to the fixed leg-segment, the hind legs do this in exactly the opposite way. The hind leg, namely, seeks to stretch out the tibia, and thus to increase the angle of the knee (R
                        3
                        ), thereby giving a push on the ground, by means of which the body is shoved forward a bit.

